id: SCA-012
title: Suspicious setup.py with os.system or subprocess
category: supply-chain
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  filenames: setup.py setup.cfg
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: (os\.system|subprocess\.(call|run|Popen|check_output)|os\.popen)\s*\(
    message: setup.py executes arbitrary commands during pip install. The Hades/Shai-Hulud PyPI campaigns used this to harvest cloud credentials.
fix: Use declarative pyproject.toml with [build-system] instead of imperative setup.py. If setup.py is needed, never include network calls or command execution.
